# Testing and verification

## Normal implementation work

Run before declaring done:

```text
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm test
npm run build
```

Pure agent-guidance / docs-only tasks may skip app verification **if** nothing under `src/`, configs, or test tooling changed - state that explicitly. Never claim a check passed unless it ran successfully.

## Prefer focused tests for

- IndexedDB migrations
- Atomic local write + outbox insertion
- Offline startup / open without network
- Failed synchronization and conflict preservation
- Provider selection (sample vs supabase config honesty)
- Sample-data operation without credentials
- Cache version upgrades
- Partial playa-pack recovery (incomplete ≠ active)
- GPS accuracy and permission states
- Simulated proximity
- Direct route refresh behavior

Colocate unit tests as `*.test.ts(x)` near the code. Use `src/test/` helpers/fixtures for shared setup.
